-- BIB 101 unit 1, part 1 of 6

alter table public.courses add column if not exists video_url text;

insert into public.courses (slug, title, subject, credits, focus)
values ('bib-101', 'BIB 101 Old Testament Survey', 'Bible', 1.0, $j$BIB 101 is a one credit survey of the Old Testament in the King James Version. Students read the Law, the historical books, the books of poetry and wisdom, and the prophets, learn the setting and message of each section, and trace God's promise of a deliverer from Genesis to Malachi. Every lesson includes a reading assignment, a video lesson script, a check quiz, and unit work in writing and discussion. The course ends with a final assessment and a final exam. Excellence, Faith, Purpose.$j$)
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

do $seed$
declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-101';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 1, $j$1.1 Beginnings: Creation and the Fall$j$, $j${"readings": [], "body": "Read Genesis 1, 2 and 3 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nGenesis means beginnings. Chapter 1 shows God creating the heaven and the earth in an ordered way over six days and resting on the seventh. Chapter 2 tells the story again with close attention to the making of man and woman and the garden in Eden. Chapter 3 records the fall: the serpent tempts the woman, both eat of the tree God had forbidden, and sin enters the world. Yet in Genesis 3:15 God speaks the first promise of a coming deliverer.\n\nKey words: creation, covenant, fall, sin, promise.\n\nYour task: (1) List the six days of creation in order. (2) Name the one command God gave Adam about the garden (Genesis 2:16 and 17). (3) Write the promise of Genesis 3:15 in your own words.\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "Welcome to Old Testament Survey. Over this course we will walk through the whole Old Testament, one story at a time, and we will read every word of it in the King James Version. Today we begin where the Bible begins.\n\nThe very first verse says, In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth. Notice what the Bible does not do. It does not try to prove that God exists. It simply starts with God, already there, already working. Everything else in Scripture rests on that opening line.\n\nThe first chapter of Genesis moves in an orderly pattern. Light on the first day. The sky on the second. Dry land and plants on the third. Sun, moon and stars on the fourth. Fish and birds on the fifth. Land animals and then man on the sixth. Notice the order and the care. God made a world that was ready for the people He would place in it. Scripture says in Genesis 1:27, So God created man in his own image, in the image of God created he him; male and female created he them. Human beings are not accidents. We were made with purpose and with worth.\n\nChapter 2 slows down and shows us the garden in Eden. God gave Adam work to do, and He gave one command. Of every tree in the garden Adam could freely eat, but of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil he was not to eat. That one command was a test of trust.\n\nThen comes chapter 3, the saddest chapter in the opening of the Bible. The serpent questions what God said. The woman and then Adam eat of the forbidden tree. Sin enters, and with it shame, fear and separation from God. We call this the fall, and it explains why the world we know is so broken.\n\nBut listen to what God says next. In Genesis 3:15 He speaks to the serpent of a coming seed of the woman who will bruise his head. That is the first promise of a deliverer. Even in the moment of failure, God was already pointing toward rescue. As you read this week, watch for that promise to grow.\n\nYour task is to list the six days of creation, name God's one command to Adam, and put Genesis 3:15 in your own words. Then take the four question check.\n\nRemember, every great story has a beginning, and every great life begins with trusting God. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$1.1 Beginnings: Creation and the Fall$j$);
end
$seed$;
